  "text": "Right, welcome back. Fuck, I have been waiting three weeks to talk about this one. Grab a drink and settle in because we are going long today. The patch notes dropped on Tuesday and honestly the first read was fine. Nothing alarming. Then people started testing it and the wheels came off almost immediately. So let me walk you through what actually happened and why the studio response has been so strange. First the timeline. On Tuesday morning the notes go up. By lunchtime three separate creators have reproduced the bug on stream. By Tuesday night it is trending. Now here is where it gets stupid. What the hell is this. Are you shitting me. This is the same shit they pulled last season and the exact same shit the season before that and I am so tired of it. It is the same fucking bug. The same fucking bug, shipped twice, in the same fucking quarter, and not one fucking person at that studio thought to check. Absolute shit show. Anyway. Let me calm down and get back to the actual analysis because there is a serious point underneath all of this. The engineering culture question is real and it is worth taking seriously. Moving on to the second thing I wanted to cover. There was a shooting reported near the venue on Saturday and the community response has been genuinely difficult to watch. The gunman was named on Sunday. The death toll has been revised twice since then and the victims are still being identified. A memorial has been set up outside and the tragedy has understandably overshadowed everything else that happened that weekend. I want to be careful here because there are families involved. So that is where things stand. Let me know what you think in the comments and I will see you in the next one.",
